rewritten-to-match: the timed encoder now follows Crystal HuffEncode step for step: frequency count, tree build with each new parent inserted before the first node of equal or higher frequency (Crystal's bsearch `>=`), codes recorded only for leaves with length > 0 or byte value != 0, then the bit packing. The original queue inserted after equal frequencies, which changed tree shape and therefore output size. The prepare step generates test data only; prep mode runs only the warmup rounds. The original version is kept as compress_huffencode_idiomatic.
